  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7560214a2c335bd4e9cc29951d82c1e3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Blond Man
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCInfoSO
  npcID: blond_man
  displayName: Blond Man
  characterFullName: No Name
  alias: Rubicund Youth
  characterCategory: Foreign Visitor / Neutral
  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1f281d7169b29604e8bf88921c35ae35, type: 3}
  description: An unnamed young foreigner who has only recently arrived in the Philippines.
    Curious and observant, he questions the prejudiced claims made by the more experienced
    guests instead of accepting them without examination.
  biography: "The Blond Man attends Capit\xE1n Tiago\u2019s gathering only four days
    after arriving in the Philippines. He explains that he came at his own expense
    to study the country rather than as a government employee. During his conversation
    with Fray D\xE1maso, he questions whether the supposed indolence of Filipinos
    is natural or the result of colonial conditions. After the dinner, he records
    observations for a work he calls Colonial Studies."
  characterFacts:
  - His real name is not revealed.
  - He has been in the Philippines for only four days.
  - He came to study the country at his own expense.
  - He is not a government employee.
  - "He questions Fray D\xE1maso\u2019s negative generalizations about Filipinos."
  - He writes notes for a work titled Colonial Studies.
  introductionLines:
  - I am merely a traveler newly arrived from Europe.
  - I came at my own expense to study this country.
  repeatDialogues:
  - lines:
    - There is much here that I still do not understand
    - but that is precisely why I came.
